He did it because he really wanted to make an impact.

2023
01:20:12.230 --> 01:20:15.440
He left, he says I got the potato lobby,

2024
01:20:15.440 --> 01:20:16.920
I gotta have the French fries.

2025
01:20:16.920 --> 01:20:19.480
I got the soda lobby, I got to have the soda.

2026
01:20:19.480 --> 01:20:23.040
And he goes, I finally I convinced I was able

2027
01:20:23.040 --> 01:20:25.640
to get wheat bread on the hamburgers, right?

2028
01:20:25.640 --> 01:20:27.360
He goes, so I put wheat bread on the hamburgers,

2029
01:20:27.360 --> 01:20:29.690
the bun, none of the kids will eat it.

2030
01:20:29.690 --> 01:20:32.980
So then I had to put a wheat bottom with a white top

2031
01:20:32.980 --> 01:20:33.923
to hide the wheat.

2032
01:20:35.352 --> 01:20:36.661
So he just couldn't take it anymore.

2033
01:20:36.661 --> 01:20:38.540
Well, you have to change the entire political system

2034
01:20:38.540 --> 01:20:42.530
to get, you know, the lobbying efforts out of there

2035
01:20:42.530 --> 01:20:44.640
that keep you know, everything entrenched

2036
01:20:44.640 --> 01:20:46.432
with the shitty food,

2037
01:20:46.432 --> 01:20:48.332
because there's too much money involved right now.

2038
01:20:48.332 --> 01:20:50.210
So it's impossible for a guy like that to come in

2039
01:20:50.210 --> 01:20:51.130
and make any changes.

2040
01:20:51.130 --> 01:20:53.863
I mean look at how Michelle Obama just got shellacked

2041
01:20:53.863 --> 01:20:57.390
for just saying maybe we should eat a little bit healthier.

2042
01:20:57.390 --> 01:20:59.020
I know, and so it's gotta...

2043
01:20:59.901 --> 01:21:01.830
Somehow you gotta have a politician

2044
01:21:01.830 --> 01:21:04.083
or a group of politicians that get it.

2045
01:21:05.284 --> 01:21:06.117
You and I have to run for office.

2046
01:21:06.117 --> 01:21:08.659
I mean that's the only way this is going to work.

2047
01:21:08.659 --> 01:21:09.830
How's your mom rubbing off on you

2048
01:21:09.830 --> 01:21:14.520
in terms of like the yoga and the spirituality and the diet?

2049
01:21:14.520 --> 01:21:16.790
Like what's that look like for you these days?

2050
01:21:16.790 --> 01:21:18.480
I went crazy with the yoga,

2051
01:21:18.480 --> 01:21:20.640
but it had to be hot yoga, as you could imagine,

2052
01:21:20.640 --> 01:21:22.741
I had to be sweating.

2053
01:21:22.741 --> 01:21:25.500
I couldn't be like sitting still and like chanting.

2054
01:21:25.500 --> 01:21:27.250
So I went nuts with the hot yoga.

2055
01:21:27.250 --> 01:21:31.050
I probably did a thousand classes or something. Love it.

2056
01:21:31.050 --> 01:21:32.990
Haven't done enough of it lately.

2057
01:21:32.990 --> 01:21:35.717
And on the spirituality front,

2058
01:21:35.717 --> 01:21:38.410
I don't know, my mom used to say, look,

2059
01:21:38.410 --> 01:21:41.993
no matter what religion, you just gotta be a good person.

2060
01:21:41.993 --> 01:21:43.220
So my thing is just be a good person.

2061
01:21:43.220 --> 01:21:44.120
She around still?

2062
01:21:44.120 --> 01:21:47.530
Gone, didn't make it.

2063
01:21:47.530 --> 01:21:49.003
She died very young.

2064
01:21:50.000 --> 01:21:50.833
Her mom had cancer.

2065
01:21:50.833 --> 01:21:52.240
As I said, she got cancer.

2066
01:21:52.240 --> 01:21:54.220
Her sister got cancer. Her cousin got cancer.

2067
01:21:54.220 --> 01:21:56.480
We lived in that neighborhood I described,

2068
01:21:56.480 --> 01:21:58.050
within a 15 mile radius,

2069
01:21:58.050 --> 01:21:59.510
there was a big garbage dump

2070
01:22:00.571 --> 01:22:02.410
and massive incidents of cancer around that garbage dump.

2071
01:22:02.410 --> 01:22:04.514
Oh, wow. Wow.

2072
01:22:04.514 --> 01:22:08.083
So diet, she preached more plant-based.

2073
01:22:09.455 --> 01:22:11.530
She introduced me to a guy named Fred Bisci.

2074
01:22:11.530 --> 01:22:12.679
I don't know if that name-

2075
01:22:12.679 --> 01:22:13.900
Oh yeah, yeah, he's John Joseph's boy.

2076
01:22:13.900 --> 01:22:16.220
My buddy, John Joseph, New York city.

2077
01:22:16.220 --> 01:22:19.630
Hardcore Ironman, vegan, punk rocker dude.

2078
01:22:19.630 --> 01:22:23.570
But he's all about Bisci, talks about Bisci all the time.

2079
01:22:23.570 --> 01:22:25.482
Guy's like, is he still alive?

2080
01:22:25.482 --> 01:22:26.315
Yeah, he's still alive.

2081
01:22:26.315 --> 01:22:27.537
He was at my wedding-

2082
01:22:27.537 --> 01:22:28.933
He's what? 92, 94, something like that?

2083
01:22:28.933 --> 01:22:29.766
93, probably.

2084
01:22:29.766 --> 01:22:32.550
He's a good friend. He was texting me today.

2085
01:22:32.550 --> 01:22:35.170
And so I subscribed more to plant-based,

2086
01:22:35.170 --> 01:22:37.190
but that doesn't mean a little bit of animal protein

2087
01:22:37.190 --> 01:22:39.150
doesn't slip in to my diet.

2088
01:22:39.150 --> 01:22:43.730
It shouldn't, but it does, but I'm mostly,

2089
01:22:43.730 --> 01:22:48.730
I'm probably 75, 80% plant based and I should be more,

2090
01:22:48.840 --> 01:22:52.304
and I fight with everybody over it, including my own kids.

2091
01:22:52.304 --> 01:22:56.600
Right, it's interesting because Spartan, which is sort of,

2092
01:22:56.600 --> 01:23:00.550
you know, kind of a cousin of like the CrossFit movement,

2093
01:23:00.550 --> 01:23:01.960
there's a cross-pollination.

2094
01:23:01.960 --> 01:23:04.253
It feels like should be raw meat.

2095
01:23:04.253 --> 01:23:07.180
Yeah, it's very kind of intertwined

2096
01:23:07.180 --> 01:23:08.480
with the paleo community

2097
01:23:08.480 --> 01:23:12.521
that's now pivoting towards this weird carnivore diet thing

2098
01:23:12.521 --> 01:23:14.736
that is confusing.
I know, I know.

2099
01:23:14.736 --> 01:23:16.940
But that's kind of the sensibility of a lot of the people

2100
01:23:16.940 --> 01:23:19.120
that are participating in your races.

2101
01:23:19.120 --> 01:23:20.350
And it's interesting that you're coming

2102
01:23:20.350 --> 01:23:21.500
from a different place.

2103
01:23:21.500 --> 01:23:24.450
Yeah, I mean Bisci, first of all, I tested it on myself.

2104
01:23:24.450 --> 01:23:28.413
I did very long distance races, like crazy races.

2105
01:23:29.350 --> 01:23:31.453
The (indistinct) by foot, right?

2106
01:23:32.458 --> 01:23:35.965
And I would carry like carrots and olive oil with me

2107
01:23:35.965 --> 01:23:37.853
and all kinds of stuff that like doesn't,

2108
01:23:37.853 --> 01:23:40.400
they don't make any sense, but I performed best on that.

2109
01:23:40.400 --> 01:23:43.390
And so I'm just not a believer.

2110
01:23:43.390 --> 01:23:48.080
That said maybe based on where you come from on the planet,

2111
01:23:48.080 --> 01:23:51.300
maybe some people need a little more meat than others.

2112
01:23:51.300 --> 01:23:52.700
I don't know.

2113
01:23:52.700 --> 01:23:57.430
But Bisci's thing is you wanna outlive your competition.

2114
01:23:57.430 --> 01:24:00.260
And if you subscribe to that,

2115
01:24:00.260 --> 01:24:02.460
I promise you plant based is the way to go.

2116
01:24:02.460 --> 01:24:04.605
Yeah, Bisci was like,

2117
01:24:04.605 --> 01:24:06.380
he was like a weightlifter or something when he was younger?

2118
01:24:06.380 --> 01:24:08.700
He was a weightlifter, and he said

2119
01:24:08.700 --> 01:24:10.340
he was going to try different ways,

2120
01:24:10.340 --> 01:24:14.150
55 years in right now on raw fruits and veggies.

2121
01:24:14.150 --> 01:24:16.230
55 Years, raw fruits and veggies.

2122
01:24:16.230 --> 01:24:18.883
Yeah, what are the big obstacles

2123
01:24:18.883 --> 01:24:21.760
that you face for yourself now?

2124
01:24:21.760 --> 01:24:22.970
Like what are the things that you struggle with

2125
01:24:22.970 --> 01:24:24.513
dealing with and overcoming?

2126
01:24:25.631 --> 01:24:28.184
Well, my biggest obstacle is I got 20 years of my life

2127
01:24:28.184 --> 01:24:29.660
invested in this thing.

2128
01:24:29.660 --> 01:24:31.820
I levered up right before COVID

2129
01:24:31.820 --> 01:24:33.770
and bought my competitor, Tough Mudder.

2130
01:24:34.790 --> 01:24:37.530
And my whole life is upside down right now, financially-

2131
01:24:37.530 --> 01:24:40.650
So how are you maintaining your sanity?

2132
01:24:40.650 --> 01:24:43.522
'Cause there so much you can't control, right?

2133
01:24:43.522 --> 01:24:45.573
Netflix and Twinkies, man. (laughs)

2134
01:24:46.771 --> 01:24:47.770
What are you doing in LA?

2135
01:24:47.770 --> 01:24:50.720
I came out to LA, I have a thing tonight.

2136
01:24:50.720 --> 01:24:52.270
This is a funny story actually.

2137
01:24:53.520 --> 01:24:56.217
Ayn Rand, "Atlas Shrugged", you know the book,

2138
01:24:56.217 --> 01:24:58.190
"Atlas Shrugged" or "Fountainhead".

2139
01:24:58.190 --> 01:24:59.770
I get asked on podcasts like this,

2140
01:24:59.770 --> 01:25:00.840
like which one is your favorite books?

2141
01:25:00.840 --> 01:25:02.912
And I'm like "Atlas Shrugged".

2142
01:25:02.912 --> 01:25:04.730
So I guess there's an Ayn Rand society

2143
01:25:04.730 --> 01:25:06.400
that reached out to me and said,

2144
01:25:06.400 --> 01:25:08.760
oh, I know that your favorite book is "Atlas Shrugged,"

2145
01:25:08.760 --> 01:25:09.880
so can you come to this thing?

2146
01:25:09.880 --> 01:25:13.670
So Laird Hamilton, Gabby Reese, maybe Peter Thiel

2147
01:25:13.670 --> 01:25:15.802
some people will be there tonight.

2148
01:25:15.802 --> 01:25:18.100
And I said, I promised pre-COVID I would be at it.

2149
01:25:18.100 --> 01:25:20.310
So I gotta go to this thing.

2150
01:25:20.310 --> 01:25:21.540
That'll be an interesting crowd of people.

2151
01:25:21.540 --> 01:25:23.585
It's gonna be interesting.

2152
01:25:23.585 --> 01:25:26.554
Yeah, how does, you know, how you look at the world

2153
01:25:26.554 --> 01:25:31.554
and think about people and potential effect,

2154
01:25:32.010 --> 01:25:34.810
the kind of people that you hire for your business?

2155
01:25:34.810 --> 01:25:37.060
Like when you're looking to bring somebody on

2156
01:25:38.160 --> 01:25:39.370
into your organization,

2157
01:25:39.370 --> 01:25:42.370
like, what are the qualities that stand out to you?

2158
01:25:42.370 --> 01:25:43.203
You know, in the early days,

2159
01:25:43.203 --> 01:25:46.300
because I just didn't have enough funding to do

2160
01:25:46.300 --> 01:25:48.573
what we were trying to do, size and scale,

2161
01:25:49.592 --> 01:25:51.033
it would be if they had a heartbeat,

2162
01:25:52.386 --> 01:25:53.390
they were good enough to work for us.

2163
01:25:53.390 --> 01:25:56.130
'Cause I was paying like $2,000 a month

2164
01:25:56.130 --> 01:25:58.840
for the first 100 people to make this thing work.

2165
01:25:58.840 --> 01:26:00.323
Expenses were just insane.

2166
01:26:02.307 --> 01:26:05.070
I would say now, if we really narrowed it down

2167
01:26:05.070 --> 01:26:06.330
a much more professional approach,

2168
01:26:06.330 --> 01:26:08.560
it's you gotta be really enthusiastic person.

2169
01:26:08.560 --> 01:26:10.862
You gotta be like, relentless.

2170
01:26:10.862 --> 01:26:12.090
I don't even care if you have domain expertise or not

2171
01:26:12.090 --> 01:26:14.183
'cause you can learn that.

2172
01:26:14.183 --> 01:26:16.410
But if you're just relentless and 24/7,

2173
01:26:16.410 --> 01:26:18.963
and just like not gonna accept no,

2174
01:26:19.892 --> 01:26:22.320
and you're honest and you've got integrity,

2175
01:26:22.320 --> 01:26:24.014
that's good for me

2176
01:26:24.014 --> 01:26:25.830
Yeah, the specific skillset can be trained.

2177
01:26:25.830 --> 01:26:27.355
I don't care about that.

2178
01:26:27.355 --> 01:26:28.220
But it's more about that,

2179
01:26:28.220 --> 01:26:29.053
it's more about the disposition.

2180
01:26:29.053 --> 01:26:30.170
Yeah, I just I want...

2181
01:26:32.465 --> 01:26:33.601
You know that, what is it?

2182
01:26:33.601 --> 01:26:34.674
Pareto's principle, right?

2183
01:26:34.674 --> 01:26:36.351
20% of the people do 80% of the work.

2184
01:26:36.351 --> 01:26:39.110
I just want more of those, I just want more of those 20s.

2185
01:26:39.110 --> 01:26:40.570
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

2186
01:26:40.570 --> 01:26:45.570
So we'll wrap this up with some thoughts

2187
01:26:46.350 --> 01:26:48.500
for the person that feels stuck,

2188
01:26:48.500 --> 01:26:52.490
who's inspired by what you just shared and is looking for,

2189
01:26:52.490 --> 01:26:56.310
you know, that little dose of inspiration to just start,

2190
01:26:56.310 --> 01:27:01.209
to get out of that cycle of analysis paralysis

2191
01:27:01.209 --> 01:27:02.750
that, you know, keeps you on the couch,

2192
01:27:02.750 --> 01:27:05.120
scrolling for the best pair of running shoes.

2193
01:27:05.120 --> 01:27:07.130
You gotta sign up for something.

2194
01:27:07.130 --> 01:27:09.430
It could be learning a new language.

2195
01:27:09.430 --> 01:27:12.190
What about when we can't sign up for anything right now?

2196
01:27:12.190 --> 01:27:13.890
Signing up for something could be as simple

2197
01:27:13.890 --> 01:27:16.310
as saying to your friend and then screaming it

2198
01:27:16.310 --> 01:27:19.230
from the rooftop, so you're committed, you're on the hook,

2199
01:27:19.230 --> 01:27:21.923
we are gonna walk six miles on Saturday.

2200
01:27:22.790 --> 01:27:23.623
I mean that could be the thing you sign up.

2201
01:27:23.623 --> 01:27:24.960
It's just gotta be, could be,

2202
01:27:24.960 --> 01:27:27.730
we're gonna learn a new language by this date, right?

2203
01:27:27.730 --> 01:27:29.390
It's gotta be, this is what we're gonna do

2204
01:27:29.390 --> 01:27:32.588
and by this date, we're gonna be held accountable.

2205
01:27:32.588 --> 01:27:37.560
And then I would say, you know, we have a prayer at Spartan.

2206
01:27:37.560 --> 01:27:40.270
Our brand has a prayer and we stole it

2207
01:27:40.270 --> 01:27:43.820
from a World War II French paratrooper,

2208
01:27:43.820 --> 01:27:45.573
who they found in the field dead.

2209
01:27:46.686 --> 01:27:47.519
They pulled the prayer out of his pocket.

2210
01:27:47.519 --> 01:27:50.580
And basically he was saying, look, God,

2211
01:27:50.580 --> 01:27:52.790
everybody is asking you for the good stuff, right?

2212
01:27:52.790 --> 01:27:54.040
They want to get back with their spouse,

2213
01:27:54.040 --> 01:27:57.030
they want to get home, a warm shower, a meal.

2214
01:27:57.030 --> 01:27:59.520
You probably don't have any of that left.

2215
01:27:59.520 --> 01:28:02.285
So I'll just ask you for the tough stuff.

2216
01:28:02.285 --> 01:28:05.850
Like the turmoil, the toil, suffering,

2217
01:28:05.850 --> 01:28:08.362
and just promise me, you'll keep it coming

2218
01:28:08.362 --> 01:28:09.770
and you gave me the strength to deal with it.

2219
01:28:09.770 --> 01:28:12.130
So like, if you can turn your thinking around

2220
01:28:12.130 --> 01:28:15.080
to more like that, like I might,

2221
01:28:15.080 --> 01:28:16.660
you and I might text you and say,

2222
01:28:16.660 --> 01:28:18.310
hey, Rich, I hope you have a day.

2223
01:28:19.391 --> 01:28:22.223
And that's like, a worthwhile day.

2224
01:28:22.223 --> 01:28:23.180
You gotta fight through today, right?

2225
01:28:23.180 --> 01:28:25.283
We don't want a complacent, easy day.

2226
01:28:26.166 --> 01:28:27.070
And so if you can change your mindset

2227
01:28:27.070 --> 01:28:32.070
to like embracing tough stuff and committing to it,

2228
01:28:32.505 --> 01:28:34.056
you just have a better life.

2229
01:28:34.056 --> 01:28:35.360
And what do you think is the main obstacle

2230
01:28:35.360 --> 01:28:36.693
that gets in people's way?

2231
01:28:37.770 --> 01:28:40.850
Well, I think subconsciously our legacy hardware

2232
01:28:40.850 --> 01:28:43.928
and software is avoiding discomfort.

2233
01:28:43.928 --> 01:28:44.980
Like it kept us from falling off cliffs

2234
01:28:44.980 --> 01:28:48.100
and freezing out in the snow and drowning.

2235
01:28:48.100 --> 01:28:49.810
And the sooner you recognize

2236
01:28:49.810 --> 01:28:52.820
that that's just like old hardware that you don't need

2237
01:28:52.820 --> 01:28:54.600
because you're not gonna get attacked by a lion

2238
01:28:54.600 --> 01:28:56.650
when you go outside or drown in the rain,

2239
01:28:57.600 --> 01:28:59.150
you gotta do this stuff.

2240
01:28:59.150 --> 01:29:01.300
Look, I have a friend who runs the largest hedgefund

2241
01:29:01.300 --> 01:29:02.150
in the world.

2242
01:29:02.150 --> 01:29:05.853
He doesn't need to do anything, okay? He's fine.

2243
01:29:07.130 --> 01:29:10.640
And his theory was no pain, no pain.

2244
01:29:10.640 --> 01:29:11.473
Instead of no pain, no gain,

2245
01:29:11.473 --> 01:29:13.270
no pain, why would I want any pain?

2246
01:29:13.270 --> 01:29:15.740
And lately he's come around to my way of thinking,

2247
01:29:15.740 --> 01:29:18.514
which is, and your way of thinking, which is,

2248
01:29:18.514 --> 01:29:20.050
you know what, look,

2249
01:29:20.050 --> 01:29:22.460
he came to Japan when I was living in Japan

2250
01:29:23.299 --> 01:29:24.170
and they had all these five-star hotels,

2251
01:29:24.170 --> 01:29:26.371
everything all lined up to do.

2252
01:29:26.371 --> 01:29:28.250
And you know what I did, I took him and his family

2253
01:29:28.250 --> 01:29:31.990
to the waterfall monks and it was freezing.

2254
01:29:31.990 --> 01:29:34.240
It was winter time, and there was ice on the mountain.

2255
01:29:34.240 --> 01:29:37.950
A waterfall is coming down and we got to go down to nothing,

2256
01:29:37.950 --> 01:29:38.783
take all our clothes off,

2257
01:29:38.783 --> 01:29:41.530
get down to basically nothing and get under that waterfall

2258
01:29:41.530 --> 01:29:44.390
and hold these metal chains while the Japanese

2259
01:29:44.390 --> 01:29:47.500
in their language are pulling the demons out of us.

2260
01:29:47.500 --> 01:29:50.170
And he said, that was the best part of the whole trip.

2261
01:29:50.170 --> 01:29:52.355
Yeah, he's not gonna forget that.

2262
01:29:52.355 --> 01:29:53.589
That was the best part of the whole trip.

2263
01:29:53.589 --> 01:29:54.740
It wasn't the fancy hotels, the fancy...

2264
01:29:54.740 --> 01:29:58.437
Like that suffering was awesome. So just do it.

2265
01:29:58.437 --> 01:29:59.787
Way to stick the landing.

2266
01:30:01.560 --> 01:30:03.929
Powerful, Joe De Sena, thank you, my friend.

2267
01:30:03.929 --> 01:30:05.930
It's great to see you.
You're awesome.

2268
01:30:05.930 --> 01:30:07.463
Yeah, that was very cool.

2269
01:30:08.370 --> 01:30:09.203
Appreciate it.

